    "International Relations\nI\nnternational\nR\nelations\nLOGIN\nINTRODUCTION\nWelcome Message\nPartners\nContact us\nDirections\nINBOUND\nExchange/Visiting Program\nOUTBOUND\n교환/방문학생\n국외연수\n단기파견\n체험후기\nNEWS\nNews\nI\nnternational\nR\nelations\nSEOULTECH\n|\nOIA\n|\nLOGIN\n학과 메뉴\nINTRODUCTION\nINBOUND\nOUTBOUND\nNEWS\nWelcome Message\nPartners\nContact us\nDirections\nExchange/Visiting Program\n교환/방문학생\n국외연수\n단기파견\n체험후기\nNews\nExchange/Visiting Program\nINBOUND\nINTRODUCTION\nINBOUND\nOUTBOUND\nNEWS\nExchange/Visiting Program\nExchange/Visiting Program\nINBOUND\nExchange/Visiting Program\nINTRODUCTION\nINBOUND\nOUTBOUND\nNEWS\nExchange/Visiting Program\nOverview\nCalendar\nCourse\nVisa\nCampus life & Living\nAcademic Credit System\nExchange/Visiting Program\n홈\nINBOUND\nExchange/Visiting Program\nAcademic Credit System\nOverview\nCalendar\nCourse\nVisa\nCampus life & Living\nAcademic Credit System\nSeoulTech Grading Conversion Table & Academic Credit System\nAt Seoul National University of Science and Technology (SeoulTech), course performance is evaluated using a letter grading system,\nwhich corresponds to grade points on a 4.5 GPA scale as outlined below.\nKorean Letter Grade\nGPA(4.5 Scale)\nPercentage Range\nA+\n4.5\n95 – 100%\nA0\n4.0\n90 – 94%\nB+\n3.5\n85 – 89%\nB0\n3.0\n80 – 84%\nC+\n2.5\n75 – 79%\nC0\n2.0\n70 – 74%\nD+\n1.5\n65 – 69%\nD0\n1.0\n60 – 64%\nF\n0.0\nBelow 60%\nS (Pass)\nNot counted\nPass\nU (Fail)\nNot counted\nFail\n[\nGrading Note]\nThe minimum passing grade is D0 (60%).\nS/U (Pass/Fail) grades do not affect GPA, and credits are awarded only for S (Satisfactory).\nPercentage ranges are approximate and provided for international reference only.\n[\nGPA Scale]\nSeoulTech uses a 4.5 GPA scale as the official grading standard.\nBoth letter grades and corresponding GPA values are indicated on the official academic transcript.\n[\nCredit System]\n1 credit is equivalent to one hour of lecture per week per semester, or two hours of laboratory work per week per semester.\nOne semester consists of 16 weeks, and two semesters constitute one academic year.\n[\nCourse Evaluation Method]\nStudent performance is evaluated based on a combination of examinations, assignments, presentations, attendance, and class participation, depending on the course.\n[개인정보처리방침]\n|\n[이메일무단수집거부]\nTel : +82-2-970-9206~7 Fax : +82-2-970-9229\nCopyright (c) SEOUL NATIONAL UNIVERSITY OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY. All Rights Reserved."
